   "text": "The pattern is matched by BaSr(FeO2)4 (mp-22427) alone.\n\n**Observed peaks.** Strong peaks are at 28.55\u00b0 (89) and 32.1\u00b0 (100). Medium-to-weak peaks are at 18.35\u00b0, 34.0\u00b0, 43.45\u00b0, 44.05\u00b0, 55.1\u00b0, 55.6\u00b0 and 57.3\u00b0.\n\n**Indexing against BaSr(FeO2)4.** I used the hexagonal cell from the CIF (a = 5.564 \u00c5, c = 8.206 \u00c5). The calculated positions match the observed ones closely:\n\n| Reflection | Calculated 2\u03b8 | Observed 2\u03b8 |\n|---|---|---|\n| (100) | 18.4\u00b0 | 18.35\u00b0 |\n| (102) | 28.6\u00b0 | 28.55\u00b0 |\n| (110) | 32.15\u00b0 | 32.1\u00b0 |\n| (111) | 34.0\u00b0 | 34.0\u00b0 |\n| (202) | 43.5\u00b0 | 43.45\u00b0 |\n| (004) | 44.1\u00b0 | 44.05\u00b0 |\n| (212) | 55.1\u00b0 | 55.1\u00b0 |\n| (114) | 55.6\u00b0 | 55.6\u00b0 |\n| (300) | 57.3\u00b0 | 57.3\u00b0 |\n\nSeveral allowed reflections (for example around 21.4\u00b0 and 37\u201338\u00b0) are not seen. I did not calculate intensities, so I assume these are weak by structure factor rather than evidence against the phase.\n\n**Other candidates.**\n- The Sr2HfSnO6 double perovskite would put its strongest peaks at 30.6\u00b0, 43.9\u00b0 and 54.5\u00b0, which does not fit.\n- The bcc CeMn4(CuO4)3 cell and the layered NaCoO2 and NaNiO2 cells would show low-angle peaks (near 16.9\u00b0) that are absent.\n- Eu4Ti3O10's main low-angle reflections (about 31.9\u00b0 and 36.9\u00b0) do not line up with the observed peaks.\n- The triclinic MnVBiO5 would give many more peaks than this sparse pattern shows.\n- I did not index Li(CoO2)2 or LiBiO2 in detail. Roughly, Li(CoO2)2's spinel-like peaks (about 19\u00b0 and 36.8\u00b0) do not fit, and LiBiO2 predicts many reflections between about 17.6\u00b0 and 37\u00b0, such as 24.7\u00b0 and 26.5\u00b0, that are absent.\n\n**Unexplained features.** A weak feature near 31.0\u00b0 and a possible blip at 10.75\u00b0 are not accounted for. Neither is strong enough to justify adding a second phase.\n\n{\"pres